course: dictionary
lesson: 13094
title: Firearm: the formal word for gun
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A firearm is a gun that a person can carry, such as a pistol, rifle or shotgun. In news reports, law texts and safety leaflets, writers use the word firearm instead of gun. «The news report said the man was carrying a firearm.» The word tells you that the object is a gun, even if the sentence does not say so.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «Laws on firearms are very strict in the UK.» Strict laws are about rules, so firearms must be something the law controls, such as guns. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap in gun and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The most important thing about a firearm is safety. «If you find a firearm, do not touch it.» Leave the area straight away and tell an adult. A gun can be loaded, which means it can hurt people even when it looks harmless.
fact: A firearm is a gun that a person can carry.
fact: Pistols, rifles and shotguns are all types of firearm.
fact: «Firearms» is the plural, meaning more than one firearm.
fact: A «loaded firearm» has bullets in it and can fire.
fact: If you find a firearm, do not touch it, leave the area and tell an adult straight away.
exercise: «The news report said the man was carrying a firearm.» What is a firearm? | *A gun that a person can carry | A tool for cutting wood | A large boat with sails | A type of bird
exercise: Which of these is a firearm? | A football | A bicycle | *A pistol | A rubber duck
exercise: «If you find a firearm, what should you do?» | Pick it up to look closely | Hide it under your bed | Take it home to show your friends | *Do not touch it, leave the area and tell an adult
test: Which word in «Laws on firearms are very strict» is the formal word for guns? | very | laws | strict | *firearms
test: Which phrase describes a firearm with bullets in it? | an empty bag | a quiet garden | a loud song | *a loaded firearm
exam: Why must children never touch a firearm they find? | It always makes a loud bell sound | *It could be loaded and cause serious harm | It is too small to see clearly | It is made of wood and might break
